    {
      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Stocks and bonds together",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Stocks and bonds together"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-akcje-i-obligacje-razem.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A **balanced portfolio** combines two parts. The classic example is **60% stocks and 40% bonds**."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Stocks** – the growth engine",
                "**Bonds** – the shock absorber"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "It grows more slowly than stocks alone, but in a crash it loses **noticeably less** – a compromise between return and peace of mind."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "How to choose the proportions",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "How to choose the proportions"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/2-jak-dobrac-proporcje.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The proportions depend on your **horizon** and on **how big a drop you can stand** without panicking:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Shorter horizon** or low risk tolerance → more bonds",
                "**Longer horizon** → more stocks"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "Test: a 10,000 € portfolio drops to 7,000 €. If you'd sell at that point – you have **too many stocks**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Rebalancing",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Rebalancing"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/3-rebalancing.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Over time the proportions **drift**. When stocks rise a lot, 60/40 becomes e.g. 70/30 – and the risk grows without you deciding it."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Rebalancing** means going back to the plan, e.g. once a year: you sell a bit of what has grown and buy more of what has fallen behind."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "“**Sell high, buy low**” – by a simple rule, without guessing the market."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
